  bootwright / status
      Report context readiness, desired state and lifecycle progress from durable records.
      While an operation runs it lists each running block's newest output file and the bytes
      written so far. With --paths it also lists the store, log, hosted and guest-image paths
      of the context on this host and whether each is present, examining no content. It
      performs no probe.

  Usage
    bootwright status [flags]

  Command flags
      --paths  Also list where this host keeps the context's data and whether each path is
               present

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright status --context lab
